# 120 Ventures – Cursor Rules

## Project Guidelines
- Use only English for naming routes, files, functions, writing comments etc.
- Use responsive design — one component for desktop and mobile, no duplicates
- Always place images in `src/assets/` not in `public/` — compiler optimization
- Commits: short, clear, imperative mood ("fix:", "add:", "refine:")
- Small, focused commits — 5 small ones over 1 large one

## Business Logic
- All operations with business logic require an API (Edge Function)
- All API endpoints should be atomic and implemented as Supabase Edge Functions
- All APIs must be authenticated and authorized — unless explicitly public
- **Do not reach directly to Supabase DB from the frontend** — always go through API
- RLS on every table, policies as simple and minimal as possible

## Package manager
- Use **pnpm** for all package operations (`pnpm install`, `pnpm run`, `pnpm add`, `pnpm exec`, etc.)
- Do not use `npm` or `yarn` for this repo unless the user explicitly requests it

## Development Standards
- Follow TypeScript best practices and maintain type safety
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling — avoid custom CSS when possible
- Leverage shadcn/ui components before creating custom ones
- Keep components small and focused on single responsibilities
- Use React hooks appropriately and avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Implement proper error boundaries for better user experience
- Validate all user input with Zod at least on the backend (frontend is optional)

## Supabase Edge Functions
- Every edge function **must** be registered in `supabase/config.toml` with `verify_jwt = false`
- Do **not** rely on the legacy gateway anon-JWT check — auth is handled inside the function
- Always use `createHandler` from `_shared/handler.ts` (provides CORS + error handling)
- Always authenticate with `getAuthenticatedUser` from `_shared/auth.ts` (unless explicitly public)
- Use `createUserClient` for RLS-scoped DB access, `createAdminClient` only when necessary
- CORS is managed by `_shared/cors.ts` via `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` env var — never hardcode origins
- Deploy/serve with `--no-verify-jwt` flag
- One function = one atomic operation

## Security
- Before any commit or deploy, read and follow `docs/SECURITY_RULES.md`
- When in doubt, apply the principle of least privilege

## Adding Dependencies or Integrations (ALWAYS follow)
- **Ask for explicit approval** before adding any npm package, git submodule/remote, or skill/plugin
- Verify source, maintenance status, permissions, and lifecycle scripts before installing
- Run `pnpm audit` after adding any new package
- See `docs/SECURITY_RULES.md` § 7 for full supply-chain rules

## Dont's
- No new packages without discussion
- No unnecessary abstractions or over-engineering
- No auto-generated doc files without discussion
- No changes to Supabase migrations without context
- No generic stock photos or random placeholder images
